@startuml
' Architecture Spec 3.8.1 — RuntimeTurn lifecycle and recovery boundaries
title RuntimeTurn State

[*] --> REQUESTED
REQUESTED --> RESOLVING

RESOLVING --> PENDING_ROLL : roll required
PENDING_ROLL --> RESOLVING : roll result

RESOLVING --> RESOLUTION_FIXED : adjudication fixed

RESOLUTION_FIXED --> NARRATING
NARRATING --> SAFETY_CHECKING

SAFETY_CHECKING --> NARRATING : unsafe / regenerate
SAFETY_CHECKING --> READY_TO_COMMIT : safe

NARRATING --> PRESENTATION_FAILED_RETRYABLE : retryable generation failure
PRESENTATION_FAILED_RETRYABLE --> NARRATING

READY_TO_COMMIT --> COMMITTING
COMMITTING --> COMMITTING : retry failed/pending command
COMMITTING --> COMMIT_REPAIR_REQUIRED : non-retryable command failure
COMMITTING --> COMMITTED : all external commands done\n+ local Adventure commit

RESOLUTION_FIXED --> DISCARDED : unrecoverable before commit phase
PRESENTATION_FAILED_RETRYABLE --> DISCARDED : retry exhausted

COMMITTED --> [*]
DISCARDED --> [*]
COMMIT_REPAIR_REQUIRED --> [*]
@enduml
